{"name":"Egg Sour","hex":"#f9e4c5","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"egg","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.","A food item shaped to resemble an egg (sense 1.1.1), such as a chocolate egg."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something).","To inadvertently or intentionally distort (the circular cross-section of something, such as tube) to an elliptical or oval shape."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/egg"},{"term":"sour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of acidity.","Made rancid by fermentation, etc."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sensation of a sour taste.","A drink made with whiskey, lemon or lime juice and sugar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Egg","blocks":[{"text":"An egg is an organic vessel grown by an animal to carry a possibly fertilized egg cell – a zygote. Within the vessel, an embryo is incubated until it has developed enough to survive on its own, at which point the animal hatches. Reproductive structures similar to the egg in other kingdoms are termed \"spores\", or in spermatophytes \"seeds\", or in gametophytes \"egg cells\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg/330px-Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg","wikidata":"Q17147"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg/500px-Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Adolphe_Millot_oeu